# Native per-expert kernels: a weight-rounding emulation arm, a measurement
# instrument. MOE_NATIVE_W_ROUND=f16 rounds each decoded weight (the product
# of its factors, in f32) to f16 before the multiply, as a matrix-unit B
# operand would; bf16 is the instrument's red. Unset, the macros expand to
# the kernels' own left-to-right product and the output bytes are 0062's.
#
